 drift from\nbefore this phase, not caused by phase-31 work. Found while running\nthe phase-gate e2e suite.","tree":{"sha":"c49715a5216cce6ff30539791273ab30272caaa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/c49715a5216cce6ff30539791273ab30272caaa8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/f0f14befd945730f43b1300bce7b4f26525959c2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/f0f14befd945730f43b1300bce7b4f26525959c2","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKGYwZjE0YmVmZDk0NTczMGY0M2IxMzAwYmNlN2I0ZjI2NTI1OTU5YzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/e43ceac87963d6872b6ae6d43bf2db7f7412d02d","sha":"e43ceac87963d6872b6ae6d43bf2db7f7412d02d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/e43ceac87963d6872b6ae6d43bf2db7f7412d02d"}],"sha":"f0f14befd945730f43b1300bce7b4f26525959c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/f0f14befd945730f43b1300bce7b4f26525959c2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/e43ceac87963d6872b6ae6d43bf2db7f7412d02d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T18:01:27Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T18:01:27Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"fix(phase-31): close FRONTEND_CONVENTIONS.md compliance gaps (F-39)\n\nOwn-code fixes: un-destructure documentUiState/draftGuard in\nToolWorkspace.tsx (§2.5), name all 5 use-enhancement-runner.ts effects\nwith Fx suffixes (§2.7), stop destructuring hook deps params (§4.2) -\nthese files postdate the conventions doc''s adoption and were hard\nviolations, not legacy debt.\n\nBuild the 3 shared wrappers the doc named but didn''t yet have:\nuse-router.ts (§5.1), shared/lib/storage/{safe-ls,safe-json}.ts\n(§6.1/§6.2), migrate their one known call site each\n(site-header.tsx, use-quality-mode.ts). Group safe-ls/safe-json under\nshared/lib/storage/ and existing use-worker-lifecycle/\nuse-pending-request-worker (F-09) under shared/lib/worker/, both with\npublic-API barrels, to clear steiger''s shared-lib module-count\nthreshold after adding new files.\n\nResolve the open Architect Review Notes decision: retroactive\nenforcement of §2.4/§2.5/§2.7/§1 across ~45+ pre-existing files is\nprospective-only, not authorized as a standalone mass rewrite -\nconsistent with AGENTS.md Scope Lock and PHASE_31.md''s ban on\nblanket rewrites without callsite evidence.","tree":{"sha":"5466a0a8fe019d26d577e699b1ca9ef577c05257","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/5466a0a8fe019d26d577e699b1ca9ef577c05257"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/e43ceac87963d6872b6ae6d43bf2db7f7412d02d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/e43ceac87963d6872b6ae6d43bf2db7f7412d02d","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKGU0M2NlYWM4Nzk2M2Q2ODcyYjZhZTZkNDNiZjJkYjdmNzQxMmQwMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/d1b358a22007a65836c180298ce6b1f07985a81a","sha":"d1b358a22007a65836c180298ce6b1f07985a81a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/d1b358a22007a65836c180298ce6b1f07985a81a"}],"sha":"e43ceac87963d6872b6ae6d43bf2db7f7412d02d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/e43ceac87963d6872b6ae6d43bf2db7f7412d02d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/d1b358a22007a65836c180298ce6b1f07985a81a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T16:28:55Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T16:28:55Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-31): extract draft-guard cluster from ToolWorkspace.tsx (F-24 slice 5)\n\nSecond slice of ToolWorkspace.tsx''s own state (F-24 literal target,\nafter F-37''s per-document UI maps): the \"confirm before discarding\nunsaved changes\" navigation guard — pending-tool/batch/reset state,\nmanual-draft dirtiness, activeDraftDirty, and the request*/discard\nfunctions — moves into use-draft-guard.ts. ToolWorkspace.tsx: 1413 ->\n1274 lines. Documented as F-38.","tree":{"sha":"040ecc60a758234a6addb807f4bbd27429c0aa2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/040ecc60a758234a6addb807f4bbd27429c0aa2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/d1b358a22007a65836c180298ce6b1f07985a81a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/d1b358a22007a65836c180298ce6b1f07985a81a","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKGQxYjM1OGEyMjAwN2E2NTgzNmMxODAyOThjZTZiMWYwNzk4NWE4MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/7f6874679c4b8619d1491973e8be7c7ffaf7278e","sha":"7f6874679c4b8619d1491973e8be7c7ffaf7278e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/7f6874679c4b8619d1491973e8be7c7ffaf7278e"}],"sha":"d1b358a22007a65836c180298ce6b1f07985a81a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/d1b358a22007a65836c180298ce6b1f07985a81a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/7f6874679c4b8619d1491973e8be7c7ffaf7278e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:54:49Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:54:49Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-31): extract per-document UI state from ToolWorkspace.tsx (F-24 slice 4)\n\nF-24 was originally about ToolWorkspace.tsx''s own ~20 useState/~18\nhandlers, not the controller hook (already addressed in F-34-F-36).\nThis is the first slice of the component itself.\n\nExtract the 7 useState maps sharing one exact shape (Record<string, T>\nkeyed by activeDocumentId: active tool, cutout mode, interaction mode,\nbackground-draft dirtiness, export settings, before/after slider\nposition, view-controls collapsed) into use-document-ui-state.ts\n(co-located in ui/, since this is presentation-tier state not business\nlogic). ToolWorkspace.tsx is now 1413 lines (was 1537), ~13 remaining\ncomponent-level useState calls (was ~20).\n\nDeliberately left the draft-guard cluster untouched\n(activeDraftDirty/discardActiveDraft/clearActiveDraftState + pendingX\nstate) - it reads from nearly every other piece of component state and\ncalls back into most controller handlers, a larger version of the\nentanglement already solved for the guided-cutout/mask-correction\nslices, but this time directly inside a 1400+ line render function.\nTreating it as its own dedicated pass is a deliberate stop.\n\nVerified: full suite (43 tool-workspace incl. ToolWorkspace.test.tsx,\n392 project-wide) unchanged, tsc/eslint --no-cache/steiger clean, plus\na live Playwright MCP run exercising the extracted state directly\n(tool switch, before/after slider, background-preset dirty state) -\nno new console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50e71cf89ff557f09f9f8fac64b7dc94afd7873e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/50e71cf89ff557f09f9f8fac64b7dc94afd7873e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/7f6874679c4b8619d1491973e8be7c7ffaf7278e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/7f6874679c4b8619d1491973e8be7c7ffaf7278e","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDdmNjg3NDY3OWM0Yjg2MTlkMTQ5MTk3M2U4YmU3YzdmZmFmNzI3OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/5aa3496c07f722b8260459e39ddb4ce1a8042471","sha":"5aa3496c07f722b8260459e39ddb4ce1a8042471","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/5aa3496c07f722b8260459e39ddb4ce1a8042471"}],"sha":"7f6874679c4b8619d1491973e8be7c7ffaf7278e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/7f6874679c4b8619d1491973e8be7c7ffaf7278e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/5aa3496c07f722b8260459e39ddb4ce1a8042471/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:38:29Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:38:29Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-31): extract mask-correction flow, fix ref-mutation lint (F-24 slice 3)\n\nPull the manual mask-correction entry/exit/commit flow (handleEditMask,\nhandleBatchEditMask, handleDoneCorrecting, handleBatchDoneCorrecting,\nhandleCancelCorrection) out of the use-tool-workspace-controller.ts\ngod-hook into a dedicated use-mask-correction-flow.ts (303 lines).\nuse-tool-workspace-controller.ts is now 690 lines, ~52% smaller than\nthe original 1453.\n\nAdding this third sub-hook call tripped react-hooks/immutability\nacross all three sub-hooks at once: direct `.current =` writes through\nanother hook''s returned object (e.g.\n`enhancementRunner.refinementContextRef.current = {...}`) are a real\nanti-pattern the rule apparently only fully engages once enough hook\ncalls exist to analyze together. Fixed by adding setter methods to\neach sub-hook (setRefinementContext/setRefinementTarget/\nsetForegroundTarget/hardResetTargets on the enhancement runner;\nsetGuidedTarget/bumpGuidedRun on guided-cutout; bumpCorrectionRun on\nmask-correction) so the controller only calls methods, never assigns\nthrough a nested property path off an unstable object.\n\nVerified: full suite (43 tool-workspace, 392 project-wide) unchanged\nbefore/after, tsc/eslint --no-cache clean (zero warnings) across all\nfour model files, steiger clean, plus a live Playwright MCP run of the\nmanual mask-correction canvas end-to-end.\n\nRemaining F-24 scope stays deferred: ToolWorkspace.tsx''s own ~20\nuseState/~18 handlers and use-object-selection.ts (1026 lines). What''s\nleft in the controller is now mostly document-lifecycle orchestration,\na materially smaller-risk shape than the original god-hook.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c1ea076a8cf4a96ac1cf86f54d1893920d9836a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/c1ea076a8cf4a96ac1cf86f54d1893920d9836a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/5aa3496c07f722b8260459e39ddb4ce1a8042471","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/5aa3496c07f722b8260459e39ddb4ce1a8042471","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDVhYTM0OTZjMDdmNzIyYjgyNjA0NTllMzlkZGI0Y2UxYTgwNDI0NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/6645ea63419cbe01ffee40b041ea894dcbc54adc","sha":"6645ea63419cbe01ffee40b041ea894dcbc54adc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/6645ea63419cbe01ffee40b041ea894dcbc54adc"}],"sha":"5aa3496c07f722b8260459e39ddb4ce1a8042471","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/5aa3496c07f722b8260459e39ddb4ce1a8042471"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/6645ea63419cbe01ffee40b041ea894dcbc54adc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:21:35Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:21:35Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-31): extract guided-cutout orchestration (F-24 slice 2)\n\nPull the guided (\"magic\") cutout target-tracking and its three async\nentry points out of the use-tool-workspace-controller.ts god-hook into\na dedicated use-guided-cutout.ts (1113 -> 874 lines on the controller,\n~40% smaller than the original 1453).\n\nThis slice is more entangled than the first (enhancement-runner):\nextractingMatte/correctionError/finalizingCorrection/retryCorrectionRef\nare shared with the manual mask-correction flow, not guided-exclusive.\nuseGuidedBrushSelection() stays instantiated in the controller and is\npassed into both sub-hooks as an input, since guided.release is needed\nby use-enhancement-runner.ts too and owning it in use-guided-cutout.ts\nwould create a hook-to-hook circular dependency.\n\nBehavior-preserving: public return shape unchanged, verified by the\nfull existing suite (43 tool-workspace tests, 392 project-wide) passing\nunchanged before/after, tsc/eslint/steiger clean, plus a live\nPlaywright MCP run of the guided auto-cutout flow end-to-end.\n\nRemaining F-24 scope stays deferred: ToolWorkspace.tsx''s own state,\nuse-object-selection.ts, and the mask-correction handlers (next\ncandidate slice, sharing the same state this one reached into).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"67ab39ac16ab1e851de0d529d0954fccb6a09b9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/67ab39ac16ab1e851de0d529d0954fccb6a09b9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/6645ea63419cbe01ffee40b041ea894dcbc54adc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/6645ea63419cbe01ffee40b041ea894dcbc54adc","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDY2NDVlYTYzNDE5Y2JlMDFmZmVlNDBiMDQxZWE4OTRkY2JjNTRhZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/1753631f3689b7940c6c7289d389bcd4b1f37bd5","sha":"1753631f3689b7940c6c7289d389bcd4b1f37bd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/1753631f3689b7940c6c7289d389bcd4b1f37bd5"}],"sha":"6645ea63419cbe01ffee40b041ea894dcbc54adc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/6645ea63419cbe01ffee40b041ea894dcbc54adc"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/1753631f3689b7940c6c7289d389bcd4b1f37bd5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T14:56:14Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T14:56:14Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-31): extract enhancement-run state machine (F-24 slice)\n\nPull the fine-detail/colour-halo enhancement pipeline out of the\nuse-tool-workspace-controller.ts god-hook into a dedicated\nuse-enhancement-runner.ts (1453 -> 1113 lines on the controller).\nBehavior-preserving: public return shape unchanged, verified by the\nfull existing suite (43 tool-workspace tests, 392 project-wide)\npassing unchanged before/after, plus tsc/eslint/steiger clean.\n\nRemaining F-24 scope stays explicitly deferred: ToolWorkspace.tsx''s\nown ~20 useState/~18 handlers, use-object-selection.ts (1026 lines),\nand further controller slices (guided-cutout tracking, mask-correction\nhandlers).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aaebf1e4a1a309476eab76c9c4dc2f4b9e1974f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/aaebf1e4a1a309476eab76c9c4dc2f4b9e1974f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/1753631f3689b7940c6c7289d389bcd4b1f37bd5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/1753631f3689b7940c6c7289d389bcd4b1f37bd5","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDE3NTM2MzFmMzY4OWI3OTQwYzZjNzI4OWQzODliY2Q0YjFmMzdiZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/363ba81361b788bbb88d6dda2ec632da09760b65","sha":"363ba81361b788bbb88d6dda2ec632da09760b65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/363ba81361b788bbb88d6dda2ec632da09760b65"}],"sha":"1753631f3689b7940c6c7289d389bcd4b1f37bd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/1753631f3689b7940c6c7289d389bcd4b1f37bd5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/363ba81361b788bbb88d6dda2ec632da09760b65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:58:11Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:58:11Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"fix(phase-31): close remaining T8 deferred findings (F-31, F-32, F-33)\n\n- F-31: describeGuidedState/GuidedBrushControls now show the worker''s real\n  download percentage during first-time SlimSAM model loading instead of a\n  static \"Preparing...\" message — sr-only announcement and visible progress\n  bar (shared/ui/ProgressBar) both fixed.\n- F-32: UploadDropzone/ChoosePhotoButton gained a revisionRef guard\n  (mirroring use-background-fill.ts) so an earlier upload trigger''s\n  .finally can no longer zero the shared preparation counter out from\n  under a newer, still-in-flight trigger.\n- F-33: __root.tsx gained notFoundComponent/errorComponent (new\n  pages/not-found, pages/route-error slices, both wrapped in SiteShell) —\n  an unmapped path previously fell back to TanStack Router''s bare\n  \"<p>Not Found</p>\". Verified live via Playwright MCP and a new\n  e2e/scenario-pages.spec.ts test.\n\nThis closes 6 of the 7 T8/architecture findings deferred earlier this\nphase (F-19''s dead-UI question was separately resolved by the architect\nconfirming intentional auto-select behavior). Only F-24 (the ToolWorkspace\ngod-hook decomposition) remains deferred — assessed as genuinely too large\nfor this bounded continuation, needing its own dedicated pass.\n\nEvery fix has a characterization test confirmed via git stash to fail\nagainst the pre-fix code and pass post-fix. Verified: tsc, eslint, steiger\nclean; pnpm vitest run 392/392; e2e not-found test passes against a real\nbrowser.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"990d44cf92dc3a8d4e8a045939f79ae636c01e6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/990d44cf92dc3a8d4e8a045939f79ae636c01e6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/363ba81361b788bbb88d6dda2ec632da09760b65","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/363ba81361b788bbb88d6dda2ec632da09760b65","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDM2M2JhODEzNjFiNzg4YmJiODhkNmRkYTJlYzYzMmRhMDk3NjBiNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/2dab2264fc1d0aaf9f96ef7b32181f0e424b687e","sha":"2dab2264fc1d0aaf9f96ef7b32181f0e424b687e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/2dab2264fc1d0aaf9f96ef7b32181f0e424b687e"}],"sha":"363ba81361b788bbb88d6dda2ec632da09760b65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/363ba81361b788bbb88d6dda2ec632da09760b65"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/2dab2264fc1d0aaf9f96ef7b32181f0e424b687e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:26:25Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T09:26:25Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"fix(phase-31): close 5 more deferred T8 findings (F-22, F-28, F-29, F-30)\n\n- F-22: consolidate the three byte-formatting functions into\n  shared/lib/format-bytes.ts (formatMegabytes/formatBytesLadder), each call\n  site''s exact prior output pinned by a characterization test — turned out to\n  be a behavior-preserving mechanical extraction, not the product decision\n  the original defer assumed.\n- F-28: usePendingRequestWorker had no worker \"error\"-event listener, so a\n  hard crash left ModelLab/InteractiveMattingLab stuck at status:\"running\"\n  forever. Added a required errorOutcome parameter symmetric to\n  cancelledOutcome; both call sites surface a recoverable error and\n  re-enable their Run button.\n- F-29: loadSyntheticCorpus''s build button stayed clickable with no busy\n  indicator; added a dedicated corpusLoading flag (kept separate from the\n  matting-run status, which the parent ModelLab also listens to).\n- F-30: MaskCorrectionCanvas''s createImageBitmap had no .catch, leaving the\n  canvas permanently inert on a rare decode failure. Wired through the\n  existing correctionError/retryCorrectionRef/CorrectionErrorAlert mechanism\n  already used for other correction-flow failures, rather than inventing a\n  new UI pattern.\n\nEvery fix has a characterization test confirmed via git stash to fail\nagainst the pre-fix code and pass post-fix. Verified: tsc, eslint clean;\npnpm vitest run 387/387; pnpm e2e e2e/home.spec.ts 16/16.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7714acfaab195092034099813cc42a1a199eb855","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/7714acfaab195092034099813cc42a1a199eb855"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/2dab2264fc1d0aaf9f96ef7b32181f0e424b687e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/2dab2264fc1d0aaf9f96ef7b32181f0e424b687e","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDJkYWIyMjY0ZmMxZDBhYWY5Zjk2ZWY3YjMyMTgxZjBlNDI0YjY4N2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/bceaa9d6dd6a5304d0cc947b1725ed761cd1e12a","sha":"bceaa9d6dd6a5304d0cc947b1725ed761cd1e12a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/bceaa9d6dd6a5304d0cc947b1725ed761cd1e12a"}],"sha":"2dab2264fc1d0aaf9f96ef7b32181f0e424b687e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/2dab2264fc1d0aaf9f96ef7b32181f0e424b687e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/bceaa9d6dd6a5304d0cc947b1725ed761cd1e12a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:51:37Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:51:37Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-31): architecture audit vs patient_tracker + full T8 state-handling pass\n\nArchitecture (F-19–F-24, docs/audits/PHASE_31_FINDINGS.md):\n- Extracted ToolWorkspace.tsx''s 4 inline sub-components (PersistentPreviewLayers,\n  MaskCorrectionSlots, UploadErrorNotice, CorrectionErrorAlert) into their own\n  files — it violated its own FRONTEND_CONVENTIONS.md §2.1.\n- Extracted shared/ui/progress-bar.tsx + inline-status-notice.tsx, deduplicating\n  byte-identical markup found triplicated across refine-foreground,\n  refine-matte, and the live EnhancementsToolPanel.\n- Converted entities/processed-image/model/types.ts (the canonical domain-type\n  file) from interface to type per §8 — narrow, zero-extends-confirmed fix,\n  not a codebase-wide rewrite.\n- ForegroundRefinementControls/MatteRefinementControls found to be fully-built,\n  tested, dead production UI (zero call sites; EnhancementsToolPanel drives\n  their business logic through a generic panel instead). Architect confirmed\n  the resulting auto-select-only behavior (no manual matte-mode or\n  foreground-cleanup override) is intentional, not a regression — marked\n  @deprecated with a removal-candidate note instead of touched or deleted.\n- Deferred with named reasons: 3 non-identical byte-formatting functions\n  (needs a rounding/behavior decision), and widening the already-deferred\n  use-tool-workspace-controller.ts decomposition to ToolWorkspace.tsx''s own\n  ~20 useState hooks.\n\nT8 full-inventory follow-up (F-25–F-27): completed the previously-deferred\nfull empty/error/warning/loading state pass across every interactive surface.\nFixed ModelStorageManager (no retry on a failed initial load — first test\nfile for this component), GuidedBrushControls (a working retry() on the model\nhook that no button ever called), ModelLab (a precondition hint styled\nidentically to real errors). Seven further findings deferred by name, each\nneeding real behavior-changing work this bounded pass doesn''t cover.\n\nVerified: pnpm tsc --noEmit, eslint, steiger clean; pnpm vitest run 379/379;\nfull pnpm e2e 77/77 (3 skipped). All new characterization tests confirmed via\ngit stash to fail pre-fix and pass post-fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"419037083c42b4e42466ae9b43f44f87cdef9025","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/419037083c42b4e42466ae9b43f44f87cdef9025"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/bceaa9d6dd6a5304d0cc947b1725ed761cd1e12a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/bceaa9d6dd6a5304d0cc947b1725ed761cd1e12a","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKGJjZWFhOWQ2ZGQ2YTUzMDRkMGNjOTQ3YjE3MjVlZDc2MWNkMWUxMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/5dcb0e138d8a08fe48637b81cff62cf511aa91da","sha":"5dcb0e138d8a08fe48637b81cff62cf511aa91da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/5dcb0e138d8a08fe48637b81cff62cf511aa91da"}],"sha":"bceaa9d6dd6a5304d0cc947b1725ed761cd1e12a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/bceaa9d6dd6a5304d0cc947b1725ed761cd1e12a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/5dcb0e138d8a08fe48637b81cff62cf511aa91da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:47:02Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:47:02Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"perf(phase-31): scope Playwright E2E gate to Chromium-only, fix real memory/concurrency cause (F-18)\n\nFirefox/WebKit/Mobile Safari dropped from playwright.config.ts to speed up\nlocal iteration (architect request). Root-caused the reported \"memory and\nconcurrency\" instability: scripts/run-e2e.ts pinned those three browsers to\nworkers:1 specifically because parallel software-rendered pages contended for\nhost memory — that source is now structurally gone with a single configured\nproject, so the run-e2e.ts serialization workaround was deleted rather than\nleft dead. Vitest itself was checked separately (--logHeapUsage over a full\nrun) and showed no leak.\n\nSPEC.md §7.4 updated and propagated via /spec-sync: Chromium is now the fast\nregression gate; Phase 33''s physical-device sample is the sole remaining\ncompatibility evidence for the dropped engines. PHASE_32/PHASE_34 flagged\nNEEDS_REVIEW in STATE.md since their scope text still names cross-browser\nPlaywright coverage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"536b4354825eabeb80ace77d1fed741e942352c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/536b4354825eabeb80ace77d1fed741e942352c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/5dcb0e138d8a08fe48637b81cff62cf511aa91da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/5dcb0e138d8a08fe48637b81cff62cf511aa91da","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDVkY2IwZTEzOGQ4YTA4ZmU0ODYzN2I4MWNmZjYyY2Y1MTFhYTkxZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/456ec96a1c1468fa0f8bd73d1ea74e659c4410c2","sha":"456ec96a1c1468fa0f8bd73d1ea74e659c4410c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/456ec96a1c1468fa0f8bd73d1ea74e659c4410c2"}],"sha":"5dcb0e138d8a08fe48637b81cff62cf511aa91da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/5dcb0e138d8a08fe48637b81cff62cf511aa91da"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/456ec96a1c1468fa0f8bd73d1ea74e659c4410c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T22:18:01Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T22:18:01Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"docs(phase-31): close out the full T2-T5/F2-F3 pass, final regression\n\nRecords the final state after continuing through T2 (profiling\ninfrastructure + heap/long-task measurement), T3 (knip dead-code scan),\nT4 (widened effect audit, found and fixed a real bug), and F2/F3 (worker-\nlifecycle dedup + the MaskCorrectionCanvas fix) at the architect''s request\nto complete every planned item rather than stop earlier.\n\nFinal full regression: chromium 77/77, firefox 76/76, webkit 76/76, all\ngreen, confirmed both before and after the last source change. Also\nmanually spot-checked the F7 upload-error flow and a real (non-mocked)\nautomatic-cutout run live via Playwright MCP.\n\nF4/F5 remain unchecked - not from time pressure, but because every\nmeasurement this phase could responsibly take came back clean, and\nfinding more would need tooling (a Profiler-instrumented build, real\nWebGPU hardware) this environment cannot stand up and validate.\n\nAlso gitignores .playwright-mcp/ (manual MCP session artifacts, not repo\ncontent).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c5879ce4a55a964c07d2742b1f2127eae454f32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/8c5879ce4a55a964c07d2742b1f2127eae454f32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/456ec96a1c1468fa0f8bd73d1ea74e659c4410c2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/456ec96a1c1468fa0f8bd73d1ea74e659c4410c2","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDQ1NmVjOTZhMWMxNDY4ZmEwZjhiZDczZDFlYTc0ZTY1OWM0NDEwYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/81f911027df825ceceadebe8449599e69ff4f27b","sha":"81f911027df825ceceadebe8449599e69ff4f27b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/81f911027df825ceceadebe8449599e69ff4f27b"}],"sha":"456ec96a1c1468fa0f8bd73d1ea74e659c4410c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/456ec96a1c1468fa0f8bd73d1ea74e659c4410c2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/81f911027df825ceceadebe8449599e69ff4f27b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T21:48:26Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T21:48:26Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"fix(phase-31): stop re-attaching MaskCorrectionCanvas shortcuts every render (F3)\n\nExtended T4''s React-correctness spot-check beyond the two files already\nchecked to every effect-owning hook/component with 2+ useEffect call\nsites. Found MaskCorrectionCanvas.tsx''s keyboard/wheel-shortcut effect had\nno dependency array at all, unlike the near-identical (and correct) effect\nin GuidedBrushCanvas.tsx - every render tore down and re-attached all four\nwindow/editor-level listeners, contradicting the effect''s own \"for the\nlifetime of the correction editor\" comment.\n\nThe two handlers passed to addEventListener are plain component-scope\nfunctions redefined every render, so simply adding a dependency array\nwouldn''t have fixed the churn. Added ref-forwarding (synced via a small\nno-deps effect, same pattern already used for use-worker-lifecycle.ts''s\nonMessageRef) so the listener-attaching effect can use a real\n[interactionEnabled] dependency array while always calling the latest\nhandler. Confirmed everything the inline releaseHandTool/handleKeyUp\nclosures touch is ref/setState-only, so this introduces no stale-closure\nrisk.\n\nAdded a characterization test verifying no listener churn across an\nunrelated re-render; confirmed it fails against the pre-fix code and\npasses with the fix. Full regression (vitest, tsc, steiger,\ne2e/mask-correction.spec.ts across all 4 browsers) passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6474f8ee609ed8a35f864162bf3a0d2e86fcba7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/6474f8ee609ed8a35f864162bf3a0d2e86fcba7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/81f911027df825ceceadebe8449599e69ff4f27b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/81f911027df825ceceadebe8449599e69ff4f27b","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDgxZjkxMTAyN2RmODI1Y2VjZWFkZWJlODQ0OTU5OWU2OWZmNGYyN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/130440fb8e93ca3781b839fe9f35fb02df6ef9e5","sha":"130440fb8e93ca3781b839fe9f35fb02df6ef9e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/130440fb8e93ca3781b839fe9f35fb02df6ef9e5"}],"sha":"81f911027df825ceceadebe8449599e69ff4f27b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/81f911027df825ceceadebe8449599e69ff4f27b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/130440fb8e93ca3781b839fe9f35fb02df6ef9e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T21:39:43Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T21:39:43Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"docs(phase-31): T3 deepened with knip dead-code scan (F-16)\n\nRan knip across the repo. Confirmed every \"unused file\"/\"unused\ndevDependency\" flag is a false positive (shell/Dockerfile-invoked scripts\nand a config-file-only import knip''s default setup doesn''t trace), and the\n~234 \"unused export\" flags are overwhelmingly FSD barrel re-exports and\nTanStack Router codegen exports - both intentional by this project''s own\nconventions.\n\nOne real candidate found: onnxruntime-web is never imported as a JS\nmodule, only referenced in CDN-path string literals. Checked pnpm-lock.yaml\nand shared/config/env.ts - strong evidence it''s a deliberate version-pin\nanchor for the Phase 22 security/license-review gate, not dead code.\nRejected removal: pulling a security-reviewed pinned dependency on the\nstrength of a static import-graph tool alone, without being able to verify\non real WebGPU/WASM hardware, is exactly the package-churn risk this\nphase''s rules forbid taking casually.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b24e1df71aa6e9c4d9579332bd5a9fad03bdc32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/4b24e1df71aa6e9c4d9579332bd5a9fad03bdc32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/130440fb8e93ca3781b839fe9f35fb02df6ef9e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/130440fb8e93ca3781b839fe9f35fb02df6ef9e5","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDEzMDQ0MGZiOGU5M2NhMzc4MWI4MzlmZTlmMzVmYjAyZGY2ZWY5ZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/d5423268cb068ff0d00c889f6656259a59c24f10","sha":"d5423268cb068ff0d00c889f6656259a59c24f10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/d5423268cb068ff0d00c889f6656259a59c24f10"}],"sha":"130440fb8e93ca3781b839fe9f35fb02df6ef9e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/130440fb8e93ca3781b839fe9f35fb02df6ef9e5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/d5423268cb068ff0d00c889f6656259a59c24f10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T21:36:24Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T21:36:24Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"feat(phase-31): add CDP-based profiling harness, measure heap trend (T2/T5)\n\nAdds scripts/profiling/measure-baseline.ts (pnpm profile:baseline): serves\nthe real production build and drives it with Playwright + a raw CDP\nsession for JS-heap measurement (Performance.getMetrics with a forced GC\npass before each sample) and long-task tracking, using the same\nmocked-worker double as pnpm e2e so results isolate React/DOM/resource-\nlifecycle cost from real ONNX inference time.\n\nRan it across two independent sample sizes for single-upload churn (40 and\n100 iterations) and one for batch churn (60 iterations, per-item \"Remove\nimage\" teardown). Growth rate decelerates ~10x from the first 10\niterations to the tail in every run, and 8-9% of iterations show the heap\ndecrease even after forced GC - the signature of one-time warm-up\nstabilizing, not a constant-rate leak. No leak found (F-15); zero long\ntasks recorded (expected, given the mocked-worker isolation).\n\nExplicitly not claiming full resource-lifecycle coverage: repeated\ntool-switching, background-fill changes, and manual mask-correction churn\nwere not exercised by this harness and remain untested.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"892cd80cc59397af0a91246b4ca7bdcfe358170b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/892cd80cc59397af0a91246b4ca7bdcfe358170b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/d5423268cb068ff0d00c889f6656259a59c24f10","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/d5423268cb068ff0d00c889f6656259a59c24f10","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKGQ1NDIzMjY4Y2IwNjhmZjBkMDBjODg5ZjY2NTYyNTlhNTljMjRmMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/0cc565f33cac6cbac8dfdbb26c04180668dd18f8","sha":"0cc565f33cac6cbac8dfdbb26c04180668dd18f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/0cc565f33cac6cbac8dfdbb26c04180668dd18f8"}],"sha":"d5423268cb068ff0d00c889f6656259a59c24f10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/d5423268cb068ff0d00c889f6656259a59c24f10"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/0cc565f33cac6cbac8dfdbb26c04180668dd18f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T20:44:33Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T20:44:33Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"docs(phase-31): close out F2 worker-lifecycle deduplication\n\nRead useBackgroundRemoval.ts, use-batch-processing.ts, and\nuse-object-selection.ts in full and confirmed none of the three fit either\nshared worker-lifecycle hook extracted earlier this session:\n\n- useBackgroundRemoval.ts has three heterogeneous concurrent request\n  trackers (a reducer-driven main process flow, two independent\n  resolve/reject Maps, and a dispose Map) with no single active-request or\n  uniform pending-map model.\n- use-batch-processing.ts is a genuine queue/concurrency-limit scheduler\n  with three separate pending Maps and worker creation tied to a\n  useEffect, not an on-demand lazy getWorker().\n- use-object-selection.ts contains two separate workerRef declarations\n  (two distinct worker-owning subsystems) using revision-number-based\n  staleness checks and explicit stale-worker-swap logic instead of either\n  extracted hook''s request-id/Map model.\n\nClosing this as reject, not defer: forcing any of the three into the two\nhooks already extracted (or building a third/fourth shared hook for a\nsingle call site each) would be indirection, not deduplication - the same\nmistake corrected earlier for the canvas-pointer-math finding. F2''s\nworker-lifecycle work is done: 4 of 7 hooks now share two real, evidenced\npatterns; the other 3 keep their own shape by deliberate decision.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"35b993b1c905579f9f90d8c964ffa86fc38046e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/35b993b1c905579f9f90d8c964ffa86fc38046e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/0cc565f33cac6cbac8dfdbb26c04180668dd18f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/0cc565f33cac6cbac8dfdbb26c04180668dd18f8","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDBjYzU2NWYzM2NhYzZjYmFjOGRmZGJiMjZjMDQxODA2NjhkZDE4Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/24f076a1e3d63d0adfa8e96b952fa00269f2eec8","sha":"24f076a1e3d63d0adfa8e96b952fa00269f2eec8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/24f076a1e3d63d0adfa8e96b952fa00269f2eec8"}],"sha":"0cc565f33cac6cbac8dfdbb26c04180668dd18f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/0cc565f33cac6cbac8dfdbb26c04180668dd18f8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/24f076a1e3d63d0adfa8e96b952fa00269f2eec8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T20:38:06Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T20:38:06Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-31): extract second worker-lifecycle hook, fix memoization bug (F2)\n\nuseModelLab and useInteractiveMattingLab (Phase 15/18 evaluation-lab hooks)\nshared a different but equally byte-for-byte identical worker-lifecycle\npattern from the refine-* pair: a request-id-keyed pending-promise Map plus\na stopWorker that terminates and resolves every outstanding request as\ncancelled, with no cancel/dispose messages sent to the worker at all.\nExtracted into src/shared/lib/use-pending-request-worker.ts\n(usePendingRequestWorker) and migrated both hooks; public API and all\npre-existing tests unchanged.\n\nAlso fixes a bug caught before committing in both this session''s shared\nhooks: use-worker-lifecycle.ts and use-pending-request-worker.ts initially\nreturned a fresh object literal every render. Every individual function\ninside was memoized, but the wrapping object wasn''t, so every\nuseCallback(..., [worker]) in a migrated feature hook would recreate its\nown callback every render regardless of whether anything relevant changed\n- silently defeating the memoization this extraction was meant to\npreserve. Wrapped both hooks'' return values in useMemo.\n\nuseBackgroundRemoval.ts, use-object-selection.ts (1026 lines, 10 separate\n.terminate() sites), and use-batch-processing.ts remain unmigrated -\ndeliberately left for a dedicated pass rather than extrapolating from the\ntwo shapes found so far without first confirming byte-for-byte equivalence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b99da01e49ec8d0ac642aa42436aa3e671fffa51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/b99da01e49ec8d0ac642aa42436aa3e671fffa51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/24f076a1e3d63d0adfa8e96b952fa00269f2eec8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/24f076a1e3d63d0adfa8e96b952fa00269f2eec8","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDI0ZjA3NmExZTNkNjNkMGFkZmE4ZTk2Yjk1MmZhMDAyNjlmMmVlYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/8b59a75d0438f81e7d3d81e1d259f001a0c4698a","sha":"8b59a75d0438f81e7d3d81e1d259f001a0c4698a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/8b59a75d0438f81e7d3d81e1d259f001a0c4698a"}],"sha":"24f076a1e3d63d0adfa8e96b952fa00269f2eec8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/24f076a1e3d63d0adfa8e96b952fa00269f2eec8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/8b59a75d0438f81e7d3d81e1d259f001a0c4698a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T20:26:18Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T20:26:18Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-31): extract shared worker-lifecycle hook (F2)\n\nuseForegroundRefinement and useMatteRefinement had byte-for-byte identical\nworker init/postMessage/terminate scaffolding (PHASE_31 F-09) — extracted\ninto src/shared/lib/use-worker-lifecycle.ts and migrated both hooks to it,\npreserving their one genuine behavioral difference (foreground cancels a\nprior in-flight request on start, matte does not) via an inline comment so\nit isn''t accidentally unified later.\n\nBoth hooks'' pre-existing test suites pass unmodified, confirming the public\nAPI is unchanged. Added a dedicated test suite for the new shared hook.\n\nThe other 5 worker-owning hooks (useBackgroundRemoval, use-model-lab,\nuse-object-selection, use-batch-processing, use-interactive-matting-lab)\nremain unmigrated — use-object-selection.ts in particular has 10 separate\n.terminate() call sites and worker-swap/retry semantics not present in the\ntwo hooks migrated here, and deserves its own dedicated characterization\npass rather than a same-session extrapolation.\n\nAlso corrects an overstated finding: the \"duplicated canvas pointer math\"\nin MaskCorrectionCanvas/GuidedBrushCanvas turned out, on closer inspection,\nto compute genuinely different quantities (backing-store pixel scale vs.\nnormalized position) — no extraction made; ledger corrected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c3e3c4f309d7ccc105b6b271eef2218dd1f7bd9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/c3e3c4f309d7ccc105b6b271eef2218dd1f7bd9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/8b59a75d0438f81e7d3d81e1d259f001a0c4698a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/8b59a75d0438f81e7d3d81e1d259f001a0c4698a","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDhiNTlhNzVkMDQzOGY4MWU3ZDNkODFlMWQyNTlmMDAxYTBjNDY5OGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/82ad1ae097a20b4fd384fb40f741a39a7823e846","sha":"82ad1ae097a20b4fd384fb40f741a39a7823e846","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/82ad1ae097a20b4fd384fb40f741a39a7823e846"}],"sha":"8b59a75d0438f81e7d3d81e1d259f001a0c4698a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/8b59a75d0438f81e7d3d81e1d259f001a0c4698a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/82ad1ae097a20b4fd384fb40f741a39a7823e846/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T20:12:50Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T20:12:50Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-31): fix upload error-state UX, harden test suite, audit T2-T5\n\n- F7: upload-validation errors now render in place inside the owning upload\n  surface (idle dropzone or batch \"add images\" row) via a new\n  UploadErrorNotice, instead of hiding the surface and relocating the error\n  into a separate grid row. Multi-file upload now aborts the whole batch on\n  any invalid file instead of silently enqueuing the valid ones behind a\n  hidden error screen.\n- T7/I2: fixed one deterministic (non-flaky) failing unit test\n  (QualityModeToggle.test.tsx, stale copy assertion); confirmed the\n  documented Mobile Safari e2e contention flake is already correctly\n  mitigated in scripts/run-e2e.ts.\n- T8/F1: characterization tests for both fixed upload-error defects\n  (unit + e2e, single and batch).\n- Suite-wide e2e cleanup: fixed 9 pre-existing failures across\n  processing-modes.spec.ts, scenario-pages.spec.ts, security-privacy.spec.ts,\n  and home.spec.ts caused by Phase-30 copy/UX drift (removed badges, renamed\n  quality-mode label, replaced raster logo with inline SVG, batch upload''s\n  \"automatic-first\" item auto-selection changing which download control is\n  visible). Confirmed all were pre-existing on main, not regressions.\n- T2-T5: real production bundle-size/paint-timing measurements and a\n  call-site-evidenced duplication/lifecycle audit (docs/audits/), correcting\n  the documented worker-lifecycle hook count from 6 to 7. F2-F5 (the actual\n  god-hook/duplication decompositions) are explicitly deferred in the\n  findings ledger pending per-call-site characterization tests, per this\n  phase''s no-blanket-rewrite rule.\n- Full regression: build/tsc/vitest (368/368)/steiger clean; pnpm e2e green\n  across all 4 browser projects; pnpm e2e:real-model passes.\n\nSee docs/audits/PHASE_31_FINDINGS.md and PHASE_31_RESULTS.md for the full\nfindings ledger and before/after evidence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"69c029170712525c40210a08497cc5622d9082cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/69c029170712525c40210a08497cc5622d9082cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/82ad1ae097a20b4fd384fb40f741a39a7823e846","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/82ad1ae097a20b4fd384fb40f741a39a7823e846","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDgyYWQxYWUwOTdhMjBiNGZkMzg0ZmI0MGY3NDFhMzlhNzgyM2U4NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/3bb365984c3ca5c52c3c2304ebec2b68f9df66d7","sha":"3bb365984c3ca5c52c3c2304ebec2b68f9df66d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/3bb365984c3ca5c52c3c2304ebec2b68f9df66d7"}],"sha":"82ad1ae097a20b4fd384fb40f741a39a7823e846","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/82ad1ae097a20b4fd384fb40f741a39a7823e846"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/3bb365984c3ca5c52c3c2304ebec2b68f9df66d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T16:14:45Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T16:14:45Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"docs(phase-31): swap phase order, add frontend conventions, extend audit scope, waive gate 30\n\n- Reorder PHASE_31 (Whole-Project Audit & Refactor) ahead of PHASE_32 (Guided Help &\n  Onboarding) at the architect''s request, since the audit no longer needs help-system\n  contracts to exist.\n- Add docs/FRONTEND_CONVENTIONS.md, adapted from patient_tracker''s conventions with\n  stack-specific substitutions and one deliberate deviation: keep this codebase''s existing\n  plain function-declaration component style instead of migrating to React.FC/arrow.\n- Extend PHASE_31 scope with T7/I2 (test-suite reliability/speed audit and fixes) and\n  T8/F7 (empty/error/warning/loading state consistency audit and fixes), anchored on two\n  concrete reported defects: layout-shifting error display on invalid-format single\n  upload, and inconsistent drop-invalid-and-continue multi-file validation.\n- Record the architect''s waiver of a formal /phase-gate 30 run so PHASE_31 (which\n  formally depends on it) is cleared to start.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8886a37dd2f6eb888df43e6966928e31e637d2ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/8886a37dd2f6eb888df43e6966928e31e637d2ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/3bb365984c3ca5c52c3c2304ebec2b68f9df66d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/3bb365984c3ca5c52c3c2304ebec2b68f9df66d7","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDNiYjM2NTk4NGMzY2E1YzUyYzNjMjMwNGViZWMyYjY4ZjlkZjY2ZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/3d62513c16a9fb3ca6e862a60f8a536349cfe650","sha":"3d62513c16a9fb3ca6e862a60f8a536349cfe650","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/3d62513c16a9fb3ca6e862a60f8a536349cfe650"}],"sha":"3bb365984c3ca5c52c3c2304ebec2b68f9df66d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/3bb365984c3ca5c52c3c2304ebec2b68f9df66d7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/3d62513c16a9fb3ca6e862a60f8a536349cfe650/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T15:05:37Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T15:05:37Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"docs(phase-30): mark PHASE_30 done in STATE.md\n\nContracts section is None for phase 30 (no new DB/API/types/env), so no\nCurrent Contract or Project Log changes are needed per the context-update\nplaybook. Gate column left unchecked since /phase-gate 30 was not run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"063229cbd18aa4bde4ce77702ff05fb4e99780a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/063229cbd18aa4bde4ce77702ff05fb4e99780a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/3d62513c16a9fb3ca6e862a60f8a536349cfe650","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/3d62513c16a9fb3ca6e862a60f8a536349cfe650","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDNkNjI1MTNjMTZhOWZiM2NhNmU4NjJhNjBmOGE1MzYzNDljZmU2NTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/63a8c12242f160f94e59525ecfd35d01489905e8","sha":"63a8c12242f160f94e59525ecfd35d01489905e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/63a8c12242f160f94e59525ecfd35d01489905e8"}],"sha":"3d62513c16a9fb3ca6e862a60f8a536349cfe650","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/3d62513c16a9fb3ca6e862a60f8a536349cfe650"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/63a8c12242f160f94e59525ecfd35d01489905e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T15:04:40Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T15:04:40Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-30): system-interface visual identity, interaction redesign, and phase closeout\n\nApplies the T23-T32 system-interface palette, mono type voice, hairline/radius\npass, Local Execution Readout, and the second-round interaction/layout fixes\n(QualityModeToggle overflow, toolbar scroll-fade, empty-state handoff\nanimation, BackgroundFillSelector sectioning, hover/focus micro-interactions).\nMarks T19-T21 complete by explicit architect decision (no need seen to re-run\nreal-model evidence, re-measure perf, or export before/after screenshots for\nthis phase) and closes out PHASE_30.md''s scope and post-phase checklist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"303198e432e4902047716f7499d07fd99953c69d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/303198e432e4902047716f7499d07fd99953c69d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/63a8c12242f160f94e59525ecfd35d01489905e8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/63a8c12242f160f94e59525ecfd35d01489905e8","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKDYzYThjMTIyNDJmMTYwZjk0ZTU5NTI1ZWNmZDM1ZDAxNDg5OTA1ZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/a0065a722dd1e497de8c802a788d777d1347f785","sha":"a0065a722dd1e497de8c802a788d777d1347f785","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/a0065a722dd1e497de8c802a788d777d1347f785"}],"sha":"63a8c12242f160f94e59525ecfd35d01489905e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/63a8c12242f160f94e59525ecfd35d01489905e8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/a0065a722dd1e497de8c802a788d777d1347f785/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T18:14:58Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T18:14:58Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"refactor(phase-30): formalize design system and redesign in-repo","tree":{"sha":"8d9351665dcb30a12a241c24cbdd6b211946bc9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/8d9351665dcb30a12a241c24cbdd6b211946bc9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/commits/a0065a722dd1e497de8c802a788d777d1347f785","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/a0065a722dd1e497de8c802a788d777d1347f785","node_id":"C_kwDOTWdiC9oAKGEwMDY1YTcyMmRkMWU0OTdkZThjODAyYTc4OGQ3NzdkMTM0N2Y3ODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commit/891ad53ead5205bbefa53499311ed0313fe57b67","sha":"891ad53ead5205bbefa53499311ed0313fe57b67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/891ad53ead5205bbefa53499311ed0313fe57b67"}],"sha":"a0065a722dd1e497de8c802a788d777d1347f785","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/a0065a722dd1e497de8c802a788d777d1347f785"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/commits/891ad53ead5205bbefa53499311ed0313fe57b67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T10:46:09Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T10:46:09Z","email":"vlad-god500@mail.ru","name":"v.godlevskiy"},"message":"docs(roadmap): insert Pencil design-system redesign as Phase 30-31, renumber 31-34->32-35\n\nAdds PHASE_30 (Design System & Redesign, Pencil-authored, design-only, no src/ change) and\nPHASE_31 (Redesign & Legacy Consolidation Implementation, absorbing the former Phase-30 batch\nworkflow consolidation scope) immediately after the completed Phase 29. Former Phase 31-34\n(Guided Help, Whole-Project Audit, Accessibility/Device Validation, Final Legal) shift intact to\n32-35. Updates SPEC.md (v1.20), STATE.md (Phase Status table + Project Log entry), STACK.md\n(Pencil/pen.dev tooling section), and forward-references in docs/legal/*.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e50f8e5c1162d10d2a9884d04b66ae489d3d8869","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6699/cutbgart/git/trees/e50f8e5c1162d10d2a9884d04b66ae489d3d8869"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avatarsik6