so they are still installed at the point in the sequence\nthey were installed before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03ffb33c2287136cf2b3ece76a6a8da2782cfb32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/git/trees/03ffb33c2287136cf2b3ece76a6a8da2782cfb32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/git/commits/221f8b4f4436a0016d0ff2426d15dac615389eb7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3399205?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha","id":3399205,"login":"mewhhaha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkyMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha/v-frame/commit/221f8b4f4436a0016d0ff2426d15dac615389eb7","node_id":"C_kwDOTXHKBdoAKDIyMWY4YjRmNDQzNmEwMDE2ZDBmZjI0MjZkMTVkYWM2MTUzODllYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha/v-frame/commit/52f88553fb5d9a38b8d1b7bc61dda244eef6beb5","sha":"52f88553fb5d9a38b8d1b7bc61dda244eef6beb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/commits/52f88553fb5d9a38b8d1b7bc61dda244eef6beb5"}],"sha":"221f8b4f4436a0016d0ff2426d15dac615389eb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/commits/221f8b4f4436a0016d0ff2426d15dac615389eb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3399205?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha","id":3399205,"login":"mewhhaha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkyMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/commits/52f88553fb5d9a38b8d1b7bc61dda244eef6beb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T13:14:42Z","email":"kopatheonlyone@hotmail.com","name":"mewhhaha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T13:14:42Z","email":"kopatheonlyone@hotmail.com","name":"mewhhaha"},"message":"Extract the document facade context into src/facade\n\nThe facade closure shares one window, document, options and a web of native\nhandles across every part of it. Make that sharing explicit so the rest of the\nfile can be split module by module: context.ts captures the native handles,\nthe tree predicates, the viewport geometry and the patch bookkeeping, and hands\nthem back as one context object the remaining code destructures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"357ebce2f04d91c525e203cb47ad50fe0318e260","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/git/trees/357ebce2f04d91c525e203cb47ad50fe0318e260"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/git/commits/52f88553fb5d9a38b8d1b7bc61dda244eef6beb5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3399205?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha","id":3399205,"login":"mewhhaha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkyMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha/v-frame/commit/52f88553fb5d9a38b8d1b7bc61dda244eef6beb5","node_id":"C_kwDOTXHKBdoAKDUyZjg4NTUzZmI1ZDlhMzhiOGQxYjdiYzYxZGRhMjQ0ZWVmNmJlYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha/v-frame/commit/bfbd8b7274778209a0d7536b8602a8cc0b584a1d","sha":"bfbd8b7274778209a0d7536b8602a8cc0b584a1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/commits/bfbd8b7274778209a0d7536b8602a8cc0b584a1d"}],"sha":"52f88553fb5d9a38b8d1b7bc61dda244eef6beb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/commits/52f88553fb5d9a38b8d1b7bc61dda244eef6beb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3399205?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha","id":3399205,"login":"mewhhaha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkyMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/commits/bfbd8b7274778209a0d7536b8602a8cc0b584a1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T13:04:00Z","email":"kopatheonlyone@hotmail.com","name":"mewhhaha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T13:04:00Z","email":"kopatheonlyone@hotmail.com","name":"mewhhaha"},"message":"Route the SSR example through the element instead of a message protocol\n\nDelete examples/ssr/shared/routing.ts and every consumer of it. The 107-line\nBroadcastChannel contract — a sessionStorage session id, a versioned schema, UUID\nvalidation, and hello/navigate-request/route-change/route-ready messages — existed\nonly because the shell had no way to drive a guest''s route. It now has one.\n\nThe shell owns the route each frontend shows and asserts it with\nframe.navigate(route, { replace: true }), which the guest sees as an ordinary\npopstate. It follows a frontend that routes itself by listening for\nv-frame-navigated and switching to whichever page owns the route the guest moved\nto. React Router, Angular, and Solid now carry no host-specific code at all, and\nQwik carries a plain popstate listener rather than a channel participant.\n\nThe specs that drove the protocol by hand are replaced by specs that drive the\nAPI: a guest that routes itself pulls the shell into the owning page, a shell\nnavigation moves a live guest without refetching its document, and a staged guest\nthat wanders is put back on the route its destination page owns. The two\nBroadcastChannel-unavailable fallback specs are gone with the mechanism they\ndescribed; the staged-failure spec still covers falling back to a document\nnavigation. Waiting for a frontend to be interactive now reads each application''s\nown hydration marker, because the shell confirms a route as soon as it loads.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0c44efe932eb3c5f26da541a918a8b88761fdb71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/git/trees/0c44efe932eb3c5f26da541a918a8b88761fdb71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/git/commits/bfbd8b7274778209a0d7536b8602a8cc0b584a1d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3399205?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha","id":3399205,"login":"mewhhaha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkyMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha/v-frame/commit/bfbd8b7274778209a0d7536b8602a8cc0b584a1d","node_id":"C_kwDOTXHKBdoAKGJmYmQ4YjcyNzQ3NzgyMDlhMGQ3NTM2Yjg2MDJhOGNjMGI1ODRhMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha/v-frame/commit/05c3b4ba7560073d5d6eeadb35900fbbea20a4e1","sha":"05c3b4ba7560073d5d6eeadb35900fbbea20a4e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/commits/05c3b4ba7560073d5d6eeadb35900fbbea20a4e1"}],"sha":"bfbd8b7274778209a0d7536b8602a8cc0b584a1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/commits/bfbd8b7274778209a0d7536b8602a8cc0b584a1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3399205?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha","id":3399205,"login":"mewhhaha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkyMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/commits/05c3b4ba7560073d5d6eeadb35900fbbea20a4e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T12:44:14Z","email":"kopatheonlyone@hotmail.com","name":"mewhhaha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T12:44:14Z","email":"kopatheonlyone@hotmail.com","name":"mewhhaha"},"message":"Expose imperative guest navigation and observe host history\n\nAdd navigate(), back(), forward(), go() and canGoBack/canGoForward to\nVFrameElement, delegating to the history the active realm already owns. A\nhost-driven route change is a same-document navigation: the guest URL changes and\nthe guest receives popstate, which is what a client-side router listens for. Every\nnavigation the host starts is cancelable through v-frame-navigate whatever its\nkind, and the methods reject with AbortError, TypeError or InvalidStateError\nrather than failing silently.\n\nAdd the past-tense v-frame-navigated event so a host router can follow the guest\nwithout polling currentURL. It fires for guest pushState, fragment navigation,\ntraversal and completed document navigation. Along the way, a staged load no\nlonger freezes the element''s currentURL after it goes live.\n\nReplace the host history monkeypatch with a Navigation API observer. The runtime\nalready refuses to boot without the Navigation API, so currententrychange reports\npushState, replaceState and traversal without v-frame touching methods that every\nmainstream shell router wraps. The host popstate listener folds into the same\nobserver, which also removes the duplicate activation a host fragment navigation\nused to send the guest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd28bbe11a4cf26e2b50e7a6c581544131171444","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/git/trees/dd28bbe11a4cf26e2b50e7a6c581544131171444"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mewhhaha/v-frame/git/commits/05c3b4ba7560073d5d6eeadb35900fbbea20a4e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3399205?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mewhhaha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mewhhaha","id":3399205,"login":"m