thubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/commits/fa703bf854f5ff1dc20ceedc0133300f23c7ff1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T18:04:24Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T18:04:24Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"feat(storage-browser): add file preview with DocumentRenderer\n\nAdd DocumentRenderer component supporting preview of JSON, YAML,\nMarkdown, plain text, code files (via PF6 CodeBlock), and images\n(inline display). Unsupported types show a \"Download to view\"\nfallback. File names and EyeIcon button open the preview modal.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"166ca42866df57f51d9fbc0b03ae6d8cf356646a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/git/trees/166ca42866df57f51d9fbc0b03ae6d8cf356646a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/git/commits/fa703bf854f5ff1dc20ceedc0133300f23c7ff1a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/commit/fa703bf854f5ff1dc20ceedc0133300f23c7ff1a","node_id":"C_kwDOTXi2CNoAKGZhNzAzYmY4NTRmNWZmMWRjMjBjZWVkYzAxMzMzMDBmMjNjN2ZmMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/commit/9571fc242be5362a71cd86a3e166bcc3db8bb8b4","sha":"9571fc242be5362a71cd86a3e166bcc3db8bb8b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/commits/9571fc242be5362a71cd86a3e166bcc3db8bb8b4"}],"sha":"fa703bf854f5ff1dc20ceedc0133300f23c7ff1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/commits/fa703bf854f5ff1dc20ceedc0133300f23c7ff1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/commits/9571fc242be5362a71cd86a3e166bcc3db8bb8b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T17:49:54Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T17:49:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: implement Storage Browser page — Phase 7 (#99)\n\n* feat: implement Storage Browser page with core file operations\n\nReplace the StorageBrowserPage placeholder with a fully functional\nstorage browser supporting S3 buckets and PVC locations. The browser\nuses the existing storageService layer (Phase 6) for all data-plane\noperations through the BFF.\n\nFeatures:\n- Location selector dropdown (S3 + PVC locations from storageService)\n- Breadcrumb navigation with clickable path segments\n- File listing table (folders first, then files, alphabetically)\n- Continuation token pagination (S3) and offset pagination (PVC)\n- Search/filter with prefix (server-side for S3) and contains modes\n- File upload with multi-file picker and drag-and-drop\n- File download via browser download link\n- Delete with confirmation modal (recursive warning for folders)\n- Create folder modal with storage-type-specific name validation\n- formatBytes utility for human-readable file sizes\n\nURL routing: /brewet/storage/browse/:locationId?/:path?\nwhere locationId is plain text and path is URL-safe base64 encoded.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Use loadFilesRef to avoid stale closures in useEffect callbacks,\n  ensuring the latest loadFiles function is always called from effects\n  and debounced search handlers\n- Replace Progress component with Spinner during upload since\n  storageService.uploadFile() doesn''t provide progress callbacks\n- Remove unused Progress/ProgressSize imports and progress field\n  from UploadState interface\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Use loadFilesRef consistently across all callbacks (handleDelete,\n  handleCreateFolder, processUpload, handleRefresh, Load More button)\n  to prevent stale closure bugs when pagination state has changed\n- Skip initial mount in search debounce effect to prevent double-fire\n  of file listing fetch on first render\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove non-existent PF6 utility class pf-v6-u-color-200\n\nPF6 does not have numbered color utility classes. Remove the\nnon-functional class names that were silently ignored.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(format): guard formatBytes against fractional byte values (#108)\n\nAdd Math.max(0, ...) to the exponent calculation so that inputs in the\nrange (0, 1) clamp to exponent 0 (bytes) instead of producing a negative\nindex that resolves to UNITS[negative] === undefined.\n\nFixes #107.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): use functional updater for setLocalOffset (#109)\n\nReplace the stale-closure form with a functional updater so that\nconcurrent state updates during Load More cannot corrupt the PVC\npagination offset.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): add error handling to handleDownload (#110)\n\n* fix(storage-browser): add error handling to handleDownload\n\nWrap the async storageService.downloadFile call in a try/catch block.\nOn failure, surface the error via a new downloadError state rendered as\na dismissible inline Alert above the file listing, matching the pattern\nused by handleDelete/deleteError.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\n- Clear downloadError on location/path change (useEffect on [locationId, encodedPath])\n- Add test for downloadFile rejection rendering error alert\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): add error handling to handleRefresh (#111)\n\n* fix(storage-browser): add error handling to handleRefresh\n\nAdd .catch() to the refreshLocations() promise chain in handleRefresh\nto surface network errors via setFilesError, matching the existing\nerror-handling convention used in loadFiles and the locations useEffect.\nPreviously, network failures silently produced unhandled promise rejections\nwith no user-visible feedback.\n\nFixes #105\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): use functional updater for setLocalOffset\n\nReplace the stale-closure form with a functional updater so that\nconcurrent state updates during Load More cannot corrupt the PVC\npagination offset.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\nAdd test for the refresh error path in StorageBrowser — asserts that when\nrefreshLocations rejects, a danger Alert with the error message is rendered.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): reset isInitialSearchRef on location switch (#113)\n\nWhen switching locations with an active search, the reset effect called\nsetSearchText('''') while isInitialSearchRef.current was already false,\ncausing the search effect to schedule a redundant debounced fetch 300ms\nafter the immediate fetch fired by the location-change effect.\n\nReset isInitialSearchRef.current to true before setSearchText('''') in the\nreset effect so the search effect treats the subsequent searchText change\nas a mount-like no-op, eliminating the double fetch.\n\nFixes #102\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): apply client-side filter for short S3 prefix searches (#112)\n\n* fix(storage-browser): apply client-side filter for short S3 prefix searches\n\nWhen searchText has fewer than 3 characters, the server-side prefix filter\nis not applied (threshold is >=3). The client-side bypass was unconditional\nfor all S3+startsWith combinations, causing unfiltered results to show for\n1-2 character inputs. Now the bypass only applies when searchText.length >= 3,\nmatching the server-side threshold.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\nAdd regression test for issue #100 to guard against the S3 prefix search\nbypass inadvertently filtering all results for 1-2 character inputs. The\ntest types two characters in startsWith (Prefix) mode with an S3 location\nand asserts that only matching filenames are displayed.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): warn when contains search only covers loaded files (#114)\n\n* fix(storage-browser): warn when contains search only covers loaded files\n\nShow an inline info Alert when the user is searching in contains mode on\nan S3 location that has additional pages beyond those already loaded.\nThe warning advises loading more files or switching to Prefix search for\ncomplete server-side results.\n\nCloses #101\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\nReplace HTML entity curly quotes with plain ASCII double quotes in the\ncontains-search warning alert. Add three tests covering the alert\nrendering conditions: shows when contains + S3 + more pages; hidden in\nprefix mode; hidden when all pages loaded.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(storage-browser): use backend maxFilesPerPage setting for PVC pagination (#115)\n\n* feat(storage-browser): use backend maxFilesPerPage setting for PVC pagination\n\nReplace the hardcoded limit=100 in the PVC file listing with the\nconfigurable value fetched from storageService.getMaxFilesPerPage().\nA pageLimit state is initialised to 100 (safe default) and refreshed\nwhenever the selected project or location changes. The test mock is\nupdated to stub the new service call.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\n- Fix response shape mismatch: getMaxFilesPerPage and getMaxConcurrentTransfers\n  now read the correct property keys from the backend response\n  ({ maxFilesPerPage } and { maxConcurrentTransfers }) instead of the\n  non-existent `.value` property that always returned undefined.\n- Fix PUT request bodies for updateMaxFilesPerPage and updateMaxConcurrentTransfers\n  to send { maxFilesPerPage } / { maxConcurrentTransfers } as the backend expects,\n  rather than { value } which was silently ignored by the validation logic.\n- Fix race condition: remove the concurrent getMaxFilesPerPage effect and instead\n  fetch the page limit directly inside loadFiles (PVC branch, initial load only),\n  ensuring the correct limit is always used on first render.\n- Add tests: verify the fetched pageLimit (50) is passed through to listFiles\n  for PVC locations, and that a fetch failure falls back to the default (100).\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c018529e9356f14f1c24348e172fe5bba317608","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/git/trees/1c018529e9356f14f1c24348e172fe5bba317608"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/git/commits/9571fc242be5362a71cd86a3e166bcc3db8bb8b4","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c018529e9356f14f1c24348e172fe5bba317608\nparent e3abc5ab2ac1111a32f56cd8e3c4f1959faf604d\nparent 27598deb01669719b4ffd6aaff19bad1e971af04\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784137794 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784137794 +0100\n\nfeat: implement Storage Browser page — Phase 7 (#99)\n\n* feat: implement Storage Browser page with core file operations\n\nReplace the StorageBrowserPage placeholder with a fully functional\nstorage browser supporting S3 buckets and PVC locations. The browser\nuses the existing storageService layer (Phase 6) for all data-plane\noperations through the BFF.\n\nFeatures:\n- Location selector dropdown (S3 + PVC locations from storageService)\n- Breadcrumb navigation with clickable path segments\n- File listing table (folders first, then files, alphabetically)\n- Continuation token pagination (S3) and offset pagination (PVC)\n- Search/filter with prefix (server-side for S3) and contains modes\n- File upload with multi-file picker and drag-and-drop\n- File download via browser download link\n- Delete with confirmation modal (recursive warning for folders)\n- Create folder modal with storage-type-specific name validation\n- formatBytes utility for human-readable file sizes\n\nURL routing: /brewet/storage/browse/:locationId?/:path?\nwhere locationId is plain text and path is URL-safe base64 encoded.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Use loadFilesRef to avoid stale closures in useEffect callbacks,\n  ensuring the latest loadFiles function is always called from effects\n  and debounced search handlers\n- Replace Progress component with Spinner during upload since\n  storageService.uploadFile() doesn''t provide progress callbacks\n- Remove unused Progress/ProgressSize imports and progress field\n  from UploadState interface\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Use loadFilesRef consistently across all callbacks (handleDelete,\n  handleCreateFolder, processUpload, handleRefresh, Load More button)\n  to prevent stale closure bugs when pagination state has changed\n- Skip initial mount in search debounce effect to prevent double-fire\n  of file listing fetch on first render\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove non-existent PF6 utility class pf-v6-u-color-200\n\nPF6 does not have numbered color utility classes. Remove the\nnon-functional class names that were silently ignored.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(format): guard formatBytes against fractional byte values (#108)\n\nAdd Math.max(0, ...) to the exponent calculation so that inputs in the\nrange (0, 1) clamp to exponent 0 (bytes) instead of producing a negative\nindex that resolves to UNITS[negative] === undefined.\n\nFixes #107.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): use functional updater for setLocalOffset (#109)\n\nReplace the stale-closure form with a functional updater so that\nconcurrent state updates during Load More cannot corrupt the PVC\npagination offset.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): add error handling to handleDownload (#110)\n\n* fix(storage-browser): add error handling to handleDownload\n\nWrap the async storageService.downloadFile call in a try/catch block.\nOn failure, surface the error via a new downloadError state rendered as\na dismissible inline Alert above the file listing, matching the pattern\nused by handleDelete/deleteError.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\n- Clear downloadError on location/path change (useEffect on [locationId, encodedPath])\n- Add test for downloadFile rejection rendering error alert\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): add error handling to handleRefresh (#111)\n\n* fix(storage-browser): add error handling to handleRefresh\n\nAdd .catch() to the refreshLocations() promise chain in handleRefresh\nto surface network errors via setFilesError, matching the existing\nerror-handling convention used in loadFiles and the locations useEffect.\nPreviously, network failures silently produced unhandled promise rejections\nwith no user-visible feedback.\n\nFixes #105\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): use functional updater for setLocalOffset\n\nReplace the stale-closure form with a functional updater so that\nconcurrent state updates during Load More cannot corrupt the PVC\npagination offset.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\nAdd test for the refresh error path in StorageBrowser — asserts that when\nrefreshLocations rejects, a danger Alert with the error message is rendered.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): reset isInitialSearchRef on location switch (#113)\n\nWhen switching locations with an active search, the reset effect called\nsetSearchText('''') while isInitialSearchRef.current was already false,\ncausing the search effect to schedule a redundant debounced fetch 300ms\nafter the immediate fetch fired by the location-change effect.\n\nReset isInitialSearchRef.current to true before setSearchText('''') in the\nreset effect so the search effect treats the subsequent searchText change\nas a mount-like no-op, eliminating the double fetch.\n\nFixes #102\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): apply client-side filter for short S3 prefix searches (#112)\n\n* fix(storage-browser): apply client-side filter for short S3 prefix searches\n\nWhen searchText has fewer than 3 characters, the server-side prefix filter\nis not applied (threshold is >=3). The client-side bypass was unconditional\nfor all S3+startsWith combinations, causing unfiltered results to show for\n1-2 character inputs. Now the bypass only applies when searchText.length >= 3,\nmatching the server-side threshold.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\nAdd regression test for issue #100 to guard against the S3 prefix search\nbypass inadvertently filtering all results for 1-2 character inputs. The\ntest types two characters in startsWith (Prefix) mode with an S3 location\nand asserts that only matching filenames are displayed.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(storage-browser): warn when contains search only covers loaded files (#114)\n\n* fix(storage-browser): warn when contains search only covers loaded files\n\nShow an inline info Alert when the user is searching in contains mode on\nan S3 location that has additional pages beyond those already loaded.\nThe warning advises loading more files or switching to Prefix search for\ncomplete server-side results.\n\nCloses #101\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\nReplace HTML entity curly quotes with plain ASCII double quotes in the\ncontains-search warning alert. Add three tests covering the alert\nrendering conditions: shows when contains + S3 + more pages; hidden in\nprefix mode; hidden when all pages loaded.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(storage-browser): use backend maxFilesPerPage setting for PVC pagination (#115)\n\n* feat(storage-browser): use backend maxFilesPerPage setting for PVC pagination\n\nReplace the hardcoded limit=100 in the PVC file listing with the\nconfigurable value fetched from storageService.getMaxFilesPerPage().\nA pageLimit state is initialised to 100 (safe default) and refreshed\nwhenever the selected project or location changes. The test mock is\nupdated to stub the new service call.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\n- Fix response shape mismatch: getMaxFilesPerPage and getMaxConcurrentTransfers\n  now read the correct property keys from the backend response\n  ({ maxFilesPerPage } and { maxConcurrentTransfers }) instead of the\n  non-existent `.value` property that always returned undefined.\n- Fix PUT request bodies for updateMaxFilesPerPage and updateMaxConcurrentTransfers\n  to send { maxFilesPerPage } / { maxConcurrentTransfers } as the backend expects,\n  rather than { value } which was silently ignored by the validation logic.\n- Fix race condition: remove the concurrent getMaxFilesPerPage effect and instead\n  fetch the page limit directly inside loadFiles (PVC branch, initial load only),\n  ensuring the correct limit is always used on first render.\n- Add tests: verify the fetched pageLimit (50) is passed through to listFiles\n  for PVC locations, and that a fetch failure falls back to the default (100).\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV8hCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtRoQABOqD8+pRc03YcFVKlKNDbPe\ns+VecDbmkHqNRJGl3wetD9KPEuPJ/K4nL1BUb7XlZt/Ip6emAeE42c/NxSmEtiDk\ng3miUKXBljoeAShNQZ70ZuKjP9opfOm1FHfUb5mTC9DAe+aKOwMFWrVK8U8ZIgqu\n5x09mef615tqr02hJ+DrDO0fJVfOZfQ5ydbwHxqaDbuQ17WUMxRFgP1H2HmksF/8\nQODOylaxQjdHrNwQvXPirXXUUy3aEmPezX8MSoDdPZ8ImSYPKPcLl9cBGbtRVvxE\nNNiZOYimuMOvFSWFHrgNT895NJMsMPkRsnSItSmBt/LLZjwTbHfeCuooNtPcK1Qz\n3pxq86dH9R4zexTTjLpo5v/MdtneAIBcOcCEmgEZo7ELYa3cFhc6z+mJdF+qmFdC\nZGvS7lTBV1hi+xEU2qUh6dtsJzat3qtFKR8V8SKURnzNxw9H2VL/V4ZZp1DMMwFM\n4SjGpf54NUrCIgf3jWr8/mzyhi+rntwYOD6bUd3moIDCyU0RPqi1/ikBPJeY/JIH\nzx25+AFyzA26ev9fWAO5JK0ZAkocl/qAmaPL+Y3SVHpfE9xssMMlcxoJXhVo7ZrI\n5pJuFz8aquPXGF4/R45ddUbSwenB16eEDrbfKn2v9xcUvEWRhrVCDE/N0aRuBJfV\nD9ONQkrhJqwaudt4IUqZ\n=iBLc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T17:49:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https: