alse,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/commits/d63c3015dcf12f984caee665664adecceb840dac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T16:45:39Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T16:45:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(storage-browser): use backend maxFilesPerPage setting for PVC pagination (#115)\n\n* feat(storage-browser): use backend maxFilesPerPage setting for PVC pagination\n\nReplace the hardcoded limit=100 in the PVC file listing with the\nconfigurable value fetched from storageService.getMaxFilesPerPage().\nA pageLimit state is initialised to 100 (safe default) and refreshed\nwhenever the selected project or location changes. The test mock is\nupdated to stub the new service call.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\n- Fix response shape mismatch: getMaxFilesPerPage and getMaxConcurrentTransfers\n  now read the correct property keys from the backend response\n  ({ maxFilesPerPage } and { maxConcurrentTransfers }) instead of the\n  non-existent `.value` property that always returned undefined.\n- Fix PUT request bodies for updateMaxFilesPerPage and updateMaxConcurrentTransfers\n  to send { maxFilesPerPage } / { maxConcurrentTransfers } as the backend expects,\n  rather than { value } which was silently ignored by the validation logic.\n- Fix race condition: remove the concurrent getMaxFilesPerPage effect and instead\n  fetch the page limit directly inside loadFiles (PVC branch, initial load only),\n  ensuring the correct limit is always used on first render.\n- Add tests: verify the fetched pageLimit (50) is passed through to listFiles\n  for PVC locations, and that a fetch failure falls back to the default (100).\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8bf8ff5c13907d28dd9832fd9229f60b2f3382ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/git/trees/8bf8ff5c13907d28dd9832fd9229f60b2f3382ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/brewet/git/commits/d63c3015dcf12f984caee665664adecceb840dac","verification":{"payload":"tree 8bf8ff5c13907d28dd9832fd9229f60b2f3382ab\nparent f5b5506d06124f564a1aab38289d1061934c7270\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784133939 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784133939 +0100\n\nfeat(storage-browser): use backend maxFilesPerPage setting for PVC pagination (#115)\n\n* feat(storage-browser): use backend maxFilesPerPage setting for PVC pagination\n\nReplace the hardcoded limit=100 in the PVC file listing with the\nconfigurable value fetched from storageService.getMaxFilesPerPage().\nA pageLimit state is initialised to 100 (safe default) and refreshed\nwhenever the selected project or location changes. The test mock is\nupdated to stub the new service call.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\n- Fix response shape mismatch: getMaxFilesPerPage and getMaxConcurrentTransfers\n  now read the correct property keys from the backend response\n  ({ maxFilesPerPage } and { maxConcurrentTransfers }) instead of the\n  non-existent `.value` property that always returned undefined.\n- Fix PUT request bodies for updateMaxFilesPerPage and updateMaxConcurrentTransfers\n  to send { maxFilesPerPage } / { maxConcurrentTransfers } as the backend expects,\n  rather than { value } which was silently ignored by the validation logic.\n- Fix race condition: remove the concurrent getMaxFilesPerPage effect and instead\n  fetch the page limit directly inside loadFiles (PVC branch, initial load only),\n  ensuring the correct limit is always used on first render.\n- Add tests: verify the fetched pageLimit (50) is passed through to listFiles\n  for PVC locations, and that a fetch failure falls back to the default (100).\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV7kzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbYYQABa0tMnyRCDOY/xddcMADbcy\nD/R/bR2Y9z1eS8FoCINeq3Oggio0DKGZMlkbftkxfECvZe3lV0REqTc5xXN7h9JU\nTqNcu8J1mAx0+iW2QzNVikRD0SsDX2eZoGPDNVyV3ba3mNW5RIkY00AVr5meoQnr\nTZDtskWepGOhHoY5bjW/06ThX30ppxZ3BaL+bDRE//2r84VKDl30sk8qGbC8m2RS\nB0KPb9iJbA18NYbKrleeOnSvySR1MEiR4XMlqjSNLss8t4PsuuX5OxpnctUGSS/0\nLmp9BC7exi5aVTK2L2lPmNfoEDRRn0I28FNXkoxvUk7w/S7CsxZ8BXKsJiVUyZoE\n4m2Frdq3CTLj3W/ltc4ZqIJTf1AiqfRfRu7XTmVRgjpRIC9onc+VGbiEwDYP+C3h\nFanwzsoDitnjsW7t3kEYi13j+7TLfgj9sQJ1ESgZcU6cduiktN5mhLR3eYGIw9xB\nUoVUsct3xqyw7sGeRUD2aFc4kuudwaSeRhqzEIM9HdJb+CGqNhRGxe2JlXdGwORh\nk+2Yw/hOOZR1uqrhqw4mskdvL9MtWgbq5J/d5sao3pyWb1vGCLWfzkjzOjX/hWJt\nkSwJqnLhCvU6DVLRKuWmaUyE8Hm5meOd7OkBbqRRLCLexU/le9UIzYCpRj4LavdX\n5d9aXcqnIyGyRiROIRFH\n=vdvW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T16:45:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/follow