os","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avetavos/realworld-mosaic/commits/4e87dcff99acb17f92424e3b72b81d83be1e1a9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T02:31:29Z","email":"avetavos@hotmail.com","name":"Aveta Vos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T02:31:29Z","email":"avetavos@hotmail.com","name":"Aveta Vos"},"message":"docs(th): de-calque Thai localisation across all lessons\n\nRewrite the Thai so it reads as written by a Thai developer rather than\ntranslated sentence-by-sentence from English:\n\n- drop the dummy subject/object pronoun \"มัน\" carried over from \"it/its/them\",\n  naming the real referent where a subject is actually needed\n- ซึ่งเป็น -> ที่เป็น, or นั่นคือ… for the \"which is why/how\" shapes\n- contrastive ในขณะที่ -> ส่วน; genuinely temporal uses kept\n- ของมัน -> ของตัวเอง\n\nTechnical terms stay in English. Left untouched: natural Thai passives\n(จะถูก…), fenced code blocks, Mermaid source, frontmatter keys, import\npaths, and every quiz answer index and option ordering.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018B4yPCa4sJQ1ue3qWrwhuw","tree":{"sha":"f6c9f2af08d169f45d7a8a8b8144a0e5cd906deb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avetavos/realworld-mosaic/git/trees/f6c9f2af08d169f45d7a8a8b8144a0e5cd906deb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/avetavos/realworld-mosaic/git/commits/4e87dcff99acb17f92424e3b72b81d83be1e1a9f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13753039?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avetavos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avetavos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avetavos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avetavos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_ur